course: dictionary
lesson: 6084
title: Big changes: metamorphosis
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can be made of smaller parts that help you work out its meaning. Metamorphosis is a long word, but its clues are in the sentences around it. «Many animals change shape completely as they grow up: a tadpole becomes a frog, a caterpillar becomes a butterfly, and this big change of body is called metamorphosis.» The words «change shape completely» tell you what metamorphosis means.
explain: Scientists use metamorphosis for the life stages of some animals. «A butterfly has four very different stages: egg, caterpillar (larva), chrysalis (pupa) and adult.» Each stage looks different from the one before it, so the change is complete.
explain: You can also use the word for a big change in how something looks or is. If Tom says, «My bedroom had a total metamorphosis after we painted it», the room was changed so much that it looked like a different room. Ask yourself: what changed, and how much?
fact: Metamorphosis means a big change in body shape during an animal's life.
fact: Frogs, butterflies, beetles and bees all go through metamorphosis.
fact: «Complete metamorphosis» has four stages: egg, larva (caterpillar), pupa (chrysalis) and adult.
fact: A frog starts as frogspawn, then becomes a tadpole, then a froglet, and then a frog.
fact: «Metamorphosis» can also mean any complete change in how someone or something looks or is.
exercise: «Many animals change shape completely as they grow up: a tadpole becomes a frog, a caterpillar becomes a butterfly, and this big change of body is called metamorphosis.» What does metamorphosis mean? | *A big change in body shape as an animal grows | A type of insect with six legs | A long sleep through the winter | Growing a new tail
exercise: «A butterfly has four very different stages: egg, caterpillar (larva), chrysalis (pupa) and adult.» Which stage comes second in a butterfly's metamorphosis? | Egg | *Caterpillar | Chrysalis | Adult
exercise: Tom says, «My bedroom had a total metamorphosis after we painted it.» What does he mean? | *The room was changed so much it looked like a different room | The room was tidied for one afternoon only | The room got smaller | The room was painted red and nothing else
test: Which animal goes through metamorphosis? | A cat, which is born looking like a small adult cat | A fish, which is never changed by anything | A dog, which grows only bigger and never changes shape | *A frog, which starts as frogspawn and grows into a frog
test: «Tadpoles breathe with gills; during metamorphosis they grow back legs, then front legs, form lungs, and the body breaks down the tail and uses it as food.» What do tadpoles grow during metamorphosis? | Wings | Feathers | *Back legs, then front legs and lungs | Gills, which they keep as frogs
exam: Which order shows a butterfly's complete metamorphosis? | Egg, adult, caterpillar, chrysalis | *Egg, caterpillar, chrysalis, adult | Caterpillar, egg, adult, chrysalis | Adult, egg, chrysalis, caterpillar
